
# Module 06: AWS DevOps & CI/CD

## 1. Git
Git is a version control system used to track changes in source code.

## 2. GitHub
GitHub is an online platform used to store and manage code repositories.

## 3. Version Control
Version control helps developers track code changes and collaborate.

## 4. Continuous Integration
CI automatically checks code whenever developers push changes.

## 5. Continuous Deployment
CD automates the process of delivering or deploying software.

## 6. AWS CI/CD
AWS provides services such as:
- AWS CodePipeline
- AWS CodeBuild
- AWS CodeDeploy
- Amazon S3

## 7. Project Workflow
1. Create website files.
2. Upload files to GitHub.
3. Configure GitHub Actions.
4. Push code to the main branch.
5. Check automated workflow in Actions.

## Conclusion
This project helped me understand the fundamentals of DevOps and CI/CD.
